claim.claim-text:
receiving a request from a client to perform a query on data stored in a database; establishing a set of permissions of the client with respect to the data in the database, the set of permissions comprising a first permission at a first position of a permissions hierarchy;
deconstructing the query into query components, the query components comprising at least one relation that identifies a dataset in the database and at least one expression that specifies an operation to be performed on the identified dataset;
identifying one or more permissions necessary to perform the specified operation on the identified dataset using a set of mutually recursive functions, the identified one or more permissions comprising a second permission at a second position of the permissions hierarchy;
determining, based on the positions of the first and second permissions in the permissions hierarchy, whether the established set of permissions grants comprise the identified one or more permissions necessary to perform the specified operation on the identified dataset; and
selectively executing the query responsive to the determination

identifying a first set of obfuscation keys associated with the first column of the pair;
identifying a second set of obfuscation keys associated with the second column of the pair;
determining whether the first set of obfuscation keys and the second set of obfuscation keys have an obfuscation key in common; and
in response to determining that the first set of obfuscation keys and the second set of obfuscation keys have the obfuscation key in common, determining that the established set of permissions grants of the client comprises the identified one or more permissions necessary to perform the specified operation

